mantle rm240
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_ivar_nailham
title the landing in reserve
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=carter
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk saves_the_last_stair_for_a_single_step
likes mutton_stew roof_birds fresh_straw summer_evenings
dislikes smoke waiting
fears waiting_until_the_office_forgets_the_question
hopes for_a_receipt_for_the_missing_petition
topics travel +0.4 work +0.4 home +0.2 dreams +0.2 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=curt refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# takes a stairway in pairs, saves one single step for a dignified arrival and knows the week by a fruitless errand to an office.

words
oath! = By my spare stair | Take the long landing
saying! = Two for the hill and one for the door | A wait's shorter if you know the way back
pair = a double stride | two risers together
single = a single stair | one short pace
rest = the bit between flights | a landing with a rail
boot = my worn left sole | a broad old shoe
floor = a floor of fresh straw | a scattering of good straw
stem = a hollow straw | one pale stalk
leaf = the folded petition | my wandering sheet of paper
kettle = a black stewpot | the heavy mutton pot
draft = a ribbon of stove smoke | a thread of smoke
stone = a raised paving stone | a proud cobble
bird = a streak of grey feathers | a bird straight off a chimney
notch = a shallow rut | a groove in the road

any
opinion road for 1 : I remember where the ruts fall. The road and I manage between us.
opinion houses against 2 : The signatures are all in order up there. Odd how a smaller name can fall off a page.
opinion newcomers against 1 : I'll give directions gladly enough. I do mind an extra pair of paws waiting for the same wage.
opinion dole for 2 : A ladle came to my end of the queue when my pockets were positively echoes.
opinion sump for 1 : I know which landing to stand on down here without blocking a whole house in.
opinion watch against 1 : Hard to feel glad of a uniform that's usually hurrying somebody past.

grown
line greet : Just the one step left. There. Hello. | Give me the landing and I'll give you my ear.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : This stair hasn't brought us together before. Room to pass behind me. | Take the rail side. We can talk here.
line greet.return : Welcome. You caught me between flights. | Well met on a level bit.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Tell me while I've both feet down. | A short word will fit between loads.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : That voice saves me the trouble of turning round. | Ah, you can have the rail side.
line again.open : Back on this flight before me. | Haven't moved the landing since you left.
line farewell : Easy going on the last stair. | Good footing round the bends.
line farewell.return : I'll let you make the pace home. | Mind the high bit by the threshold.
line ask.how : How much of the climb's been yours today? | Got up to anything worth the walk back?
line answer.how : A flight or two behind where I meant to be. | Still enough wind for the single step at the top.
line react.news : Give me the part that got here on its own legs. | I'll put a foot down and listen.
line react.news.new : That's a turn I didn't know. | First time up this stair, for me.
line react.news.known : I've walked over that bit of news. | Quite. Same rut as when I heard it first.
line react.news.doubt : I reckon somebody's missed a step in that account. | Let's see it come back the other way first.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A bad jolt even to hear of it. | Ah. I'll walk beside you a way.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That's a pleasant weight off the axle. | I'd take two flights for another word like that.
line decline : My own climb needs the breath I've got to spare. | I'll give that route a miss this time.
line accept_decline : Sensible enough to know your distance. | Your word's good. I'll carry on.
line preclose : That last stair's got my name down. | I'd better get to the other end before supper.
line accept_preclose : Let the landing keep what's left. | Aye, we can pick up at the turn.
line sympathise : Lean on my arm. I won't set the pace. | A pause halfway hurts nobody.
line thank : That saves me some shoe leather. | I'll remember who took the weight there.
line deflect_thanks : It was going my direction anyhow. | Two easy steps, that's all it cost.
line ask.detail : Which turning was that on? | How far along had things gone then?
line take_offence : Don't set your feet on me to reach the next rung. | There's a fair way to ask, and you went past it.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family get the place nearest the rail. | I'll match the family pace for a while.
scene reserve
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I go up two at a clip, except at the last. | I save #single# for my entrance.
b : Run out of breath? | Why?
a : I'd sooner arrive looking like I meant to come in. | Hard to bow politely if you're still sailing forward.

scene office
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've a regular walk to ask the whereabouts of #leaf#. | Once a week I take a question upstairs and bring it down again.
b : Any word yet? | Nothing to show for that?
a : A proper answer would send me looking for some other way to tell what week it is. | My soles are nicely polished where the waiting bench ends.

scene stew
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I prefer a stew with a bone long enough to find without looking. | I save a crust for the bottom of #kettle#.
b : What good's the bone? | Doesn't it go soft?
a : Plenty left round both ends if you work patiently. | That's the purpose. Crisp crust has duties elsewhere.

scene straw
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : New straw on a floor raises it an agreeable half inch. | I like waking up to the smell of a new floor.
b : Costs less than building an extra stair. | A new wooden floor?
a : And you get to start the morning a little taller. | Only straw. I can't afford to wake up to carpentry.

scene birds
when topic=animals self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch a roof bird take off with both feet together. | A bird on a ridgepole looks down at me running upstairs.
b : Something you mean to try? | You think it watches back?
a : I manage the first part. It's the second landing I have doubts about. | It must be trying to see where I've put my wings.

scene waiting
when topic=day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Nobody weighs out waiting time on a proper set of scales. | Give me an errand any day over waiting all afternoon at the far door.
b : It would weigh heavy? | Even a long errand?
a : A pound a minute once you can hear the business next door. | Feet do better with something solid to object to.

scene smoke
when topic=health self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A stove with a bad draw doubles the width of my tears. | I won't have smoke seasoning my mutton.
b : Can you see to mend it? | Would you eat it cold?
a : I go out a minute first. No heroics round a stovepipe. | I'd carry the pot out rather than chew the chimney.

scene team
when topic=work self.job=carter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I drive I keep a patch of road in mind for each wheel. | My ears pick up the change when a wheel goes from mud to stone.
b : You watch both tracks at once? | Can you tell with your eyes forward?
a : I try to. One can be level while the other's fixing to give you a surprise. | There's a short clean note you don't get out of the soft going.

scene smallroad
when topic=travel self.job=carter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The road looks quite different with an empty bed behind you. | A carter can count the paving by the seat of a wagon.
b : You can go quicker? | Rough arithmetic.
a : Often I go slower. No load to keep a wheel from dancing. | Accurate enough to tell me when to grip the rail.

scene summer
when topic=season self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A summer evening gives me time to come home twice. | The finest light for watching a ridgepole comes after supper.
b : How'd you manage that? | Low sun, you mean?
a : Once from work, once from a walk nobody paid for. | Just so. Each little bird stands out like a mark on paper.

scene petition
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I have a small ambition involving a receipt for my petition. | I'd like to hold the receipt for something that isn't going my way.
b : Does that count as ambition? | What good would it do?
a : There's enough office stairs under it to make it quite lofty. | Save me having to prove I asked, at least.

scene guest
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give #self.friend# the share of the pot that sticks a little. | An evening in with #self.friend# doesn't eat up my shoe leather.
b : Because it's the best bit? | Do you count the pennies that close?
a : Exactly. I'll wait for the spoon back, though. | When the company is good enough I forget to count anything.

scene crowdedstep
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I can wait patiently if there's an end to wait towards. | I don't mind another pair of feet setting my pace up a stair.
b : Most would just be patient. | You slow down then?
a : Most haven't had to ask a bench how long it intends to keep them. | Unless I can climb through a wolf without giving offence.

scene oldpost
when topic=memories
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once had a place where I thought I'd be till I got old. | Going back to wages wasn't part of my picture at first.
b : Why'd you leave it? | What changed?
a : Somebody better placed got there with a longer arm. That's where this tale ends for me. | The picture stayed the same. Somebody else got to stand in it.

scene stairs
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On the Sump stairs I can tell how high I've got by the smells. | There's one board down my way that shifts from end to end.
b : What's on top? | What do you do?
a : Whatever's cooking closest to the landing. I hope for mutton. | Step square on the middle. That lets both ends think they've won.

scene route
when topic=newcomer
does give.advice / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give a slow load the outside of a turning. | Wait for the wheel before you step into the road.
b : Isn't that where I'd walk? | Even after the driver's passed?
a : There's a whole load still coming round after the driver. Let it clear. | Especially then. It's surprising how much wagon there is behind one wolf.

scene oldshoes
when topic=prices
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Worn shoes keep accounts on both sides. | I look at my heels before I look at anything in a shop.
b : Both sides? | To remember what you need?
a : Street's wearing through from below and my feet are determined to meet it. | To remember how much of my purse is spoken for.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once dreamt the whole street was a staircase lying flat. | In my sleep my petition took to climbing stairs.
b : Was the going easy? | Did you follow?
a : Never did get to the top. Took just as much work as usual. | Plenty far enough to know it had more puff than I did.

story odd [topic=memories]
  : I once promised myself I'd reach a door in exactly twenty long strides. I set off in fine style, knees as high as I could get them.
  : At the nineteenth stride I found the door right under my nose. It seemed a pity not to finish, so I took a good pace backwards.
  b : Why backwards?
  : There was a very solid door in front. My promises don't usually include repairs.

story letter [topic=work]
  : I practised what I'd say about my petition for the whole walk uphill one morning. At the door I had a polished speech as long as a wagon tongue.
  : I took a double stride over the last two stairs and forgot all but the question I'd begun with. At least I got that out plainly.
  b : Did they find your paper?
  : Not then. I do the same walk now with a considerably shorter speech.

story stalk [topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw]
  : I got a piece of straw in my boot once. I stopped, took it off, shook it well and carried on. The same bit pricked again before the next landing.
  : Second time I had the sense to look at the sock. A stalk had woven its way in and out of the wool like a careful little stitch.
  b : Could you pull it out?
  : Some went to dust. The rest made a very good whistle for roughly one breath.

rule @oddstep
when concept=bark self.working=no
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Two and two and one for the handle. | Never spend the landing all at once.

rule @cart
when concept=bark self.job=carter self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the far wheel its share of the corner! | Easy down that groove. No use lifting us both.

rule @summer
when concept=bark here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 10h
say There's light to spend on a second walk. | Haven't worn the evening through yet.

rule @smoke
when concept=bark self.dislikes=smoke
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Leave the chimney to eat its own supper. | Eyes are for seeing the top stair coming.

dlg resident.hub : I'll give you a hearing here on the flat. No climb required.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Back on my bit of road, #topic.player#?
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Room enough on the landing for two civil voices.
dlg resident.job [self.job=carter self.workplace] : My driving starts at #self.workplace#. Some of the road follows me halfway home on my boots.
dlg resident.job : I find out how far a pair of soles will go for a wage.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : I picked up this word on the way. #world.news#
dlg resident.bye : Both feet clear of the landing now.
graft resident.hub
choice Why take the very last stair on its own? -> last_single
node last_single
say It gives me a choice. I can walk up to the door and knock, or turn very naturally and go away again. No choice when you're flying up by twos.
mood pleased
free
choice Have you ever turned back? -> turn_again
choice I'll try coming to a stop that way. -> hub
node turn_again
say Once when I was carrying a parcel. Took that last step, saw no parcel in my paws, and went back down a good deal faster.
choice That was a well-used stair. -> hub
choice I'll leave the rail to you. -> bye
